Description: Read a tag name once, in the tag states, and carry it on the token
 The open tag start and close tag tokens carry the element name, read as the
 tag name state reads it: HTML characters lower-cased up to whitespace, "/"
 or ">", a template glued after the name ends it, and a template right after
 the opening is the name. The tree reads the name from the token and pairs
 close tags by it, ignoring whitespace inside template text. So "</ div>"
 closes nothing, "</d iv>" is "</d>", "</div class>" closes a div, and
 "</{{ Tag }}>" does not close "<{{ tag }}>". "<" opens a tag only before an
 ASCII letter, so "x <3" is text. Token types and contexts are looked up in a
 Map, so "<constructor>" no longer crashes the parser. parseOpenTagName and
 parseCloseTagName, and their tests, are replaced.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/parse-for-eslint.test.ts ("markup read as a browser reads it"); npm run test:upstream (snapshots gain "name")
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
